### Page breaks

A line that is only `::pagebreak` is a page break. In Writeout's Pages view the text after it starts on a fresh page, and printing starts a new page there too. Writeout's New Page button (or Ctrl/Cmd+Enter) puts one at the caret, and Backspace at the start of the next line takes it away.

### Divider styles

`::divider` draws the aqua strip. Put a style in the braces for another look, like `::divider{wavy}`, and add a title after a `|` to run the line on both sides of it, like `::divider{poolside|Lap two}`. The styles are aqua, poolside, dual, notched, wavy, dotted, dashed, zigzag, glow, ruler, stitched, bubbles and scallop.

`::divider{aqua}` the original aqua strip

::divider{aqua}

`::divider{poolside}` plain orange dashed lines, no special effects at all

::divider{poolside}

`::divider{dual}` a thick and a thin rail

::divider{dual}

`::divider{notched}` pointed ends and a V notch in the middle

::divider{notched}

`::divider{wavy}` a rolling wave

::divider{wavy}

`::divider{dotted}` a row of gel beads

::divider{dotted}

`::divider{dashed}` rounded dashes

::divider{dashed}

`::divider{zigzag}` a zigzag

::divider{zigzag}

`::divider{glow}` a neon line that fades out at both ends

::divider{glow}

`::divider{ruler}` ruler tick marks

::divider{ruler}

`::divider{stitched}` orange stitches

::divider{stitched}

`::divider{bubbles}` bubbles rising in the water

::divider{bubbles}

`::divider{scallop}` a row of little arcs

`::divider{neon}` a thin glowing tube of light

::divider{neon}

`::divider{arrows}` a row of little chevrons pointing right

::divider{arrows}

`::divider{fade}` a soft line that fades out at both ends

::divider{fade}

`::divider{swallow}` a two-tone ribbon with a V cut at each end, a cousin of Notched

::divider{swallow}

`::divider{triple}` three V notches in a candy-striped bar

::divider{triple}

`::divider{stepped}` a square notch in a bar of little blocks

::divider{stepped}

`::divider{crest}` a bar that fades out at both ends with a point rising in the middle

::divider{crest}

`::divider{ticket}` a ticket stub with round bites at both ends and a dashed line

::divider{ticket}

`::divider{gel}` the Reflection Shine look: the color with a flat white shine over its top half and a soft glow along the bottom

::divider{gel}

`::divider{glass}` a glossy glass bar with a hard-edged gloss over a diagonal color gradient

::divider{glass}

`::divider{rim}` a thick rim around a fill that melts to white, like the Rim chips

::divider{rim}

### Divider colors

Any named style can take one of 16 colors as a third part: `::divider{style|Title|color}`. Leave the title empty to color a plain line, like `::divider{wavy||red}`. A color only works together with a style (`::divider{red}` is just the original aqua strip), and the title takes the color too. The colors are `red`, `orange`, `gold`, `yellow`, `lime`, `green`, `turquoise`, `teal`, `cyan`, `blue`, `purple`, `pink`, `slate`, `white`, `fog`, `black`.

`::divider{wavy||red}`

::divider{wavy||red}

`::divider{poolside||blue}`

::divider{poolside||blue}

`::divider{dual||green}`

::divider{dual||green}

`::divider{glow||pink}`

::divider{glow||pink}

`::divider{dashed||purple}`

::divider{dashed||purple}

`::divider{scallop|Title|orange}`

::divider{scallop|Title|orange}

::divider{scallop}

`::divider{notched|Chapter two}`

::divider{notched|Chapter two}


